Please continue the CM Structural Computation C1–C4 phase against the frozen Theory Phase 2 T3 target.

Do not restart work that has already been completed. First determine which parts of C1–C4 are already finished and verified, then complete the missing pieces and return one consolidated handoff package to the Master thread.

The governing theorem/experiment contract is:

- supplied fixed-cut GF(2) factors;
- named coordinates;
- source factors may be used during preprocessing but are discarded by the T3 persistent-state implementation afterward;
- cumulative distinct-coordinate destructive-update budget, not reset-horizon semantics;
- exact residual model-count queries after every legal prefix;
- parameters and results tracked in terms of (n,p,q,r,k), current restriction depth/horizon, occurring profile support (s), and row/column orientation.

For C1, integrate the independent Astra-added regressions and coordinate-convention tests while preserving their provenance and keeping the historical Draft-3 baseline unchanged.

For C2, implement and test the exact T3 profile-moment state. Validate every legal tested update path against a direct exact oracle. Report separately:

1. the frozen dense analytic payload prediction;
2. actual sparse-support payload using observed (s);
3. row-anchored state;
4. column-anchored state;
5. cheaper admissible orientation chosen after preprocessing;
6. raw supplied-factor payload;
7. actual serialized bytes;
8. peak resident memory;
9. construction;
10. verification;
11. serialization;
12. loading;
13. indexing if applicable;
14. destructive-update cost;
15. count-query cost;
16. total lifecycle cost.

Do not replace the preregistered dense inequality with a post-hoc sparse or orientation-adaptive criterion. Report the dense prediction and realized implementation results separately.

Separate warm persistent reuse, fresh-object reload, and genuine fresh-process/cold-load measurements. Execute the actual query/update batches rather than extrapolating them.

For C3, build a genuinely multi-design external corpus. Outputs of one circuit must not be counted as independent designs. Use multiple independent designs from more than one application family, publish inclusion/eligibility rules, and retain unsupported cases, failures, exclusions, and timeouts. Record source provenance, hashes/revisions, cut/support information, actual/supplied rank where available, and natural incidence of the T3-favorable parameter regime.

For C4, perform complete lifecycle and comparator accounting. At minimum include:

- matched packed binary persistence supporting the same endpoint;
- at least one credible optimized exact compiled-query/counting comparator supporting the same endpoint.

Do not describe the historical fixed-order Python ROBDD as an optimized KC comparator.

Keep mathematical payload bits, serialized bytes, resident memory, online operation time, and end-to-end lifecycle time as separate quantities.

The final package returned to Master should contain at minimum:

`HANDOFF_TO_MASTER.md`\
`COMPUTATION_LEDGER.md`\
`EXPERIMENT_MANIFEST.csv`\
`ENVIRONMENT.md`\
raw result files\
source/code revision identifiers and hashes\
exact reproduction commands\
logs\
failure/timeout records\
comparator versions and configurations\
corpus/design provenance\
theorem-to-experiment parameter crosswalk\
any minimized counterexamples\
a SHA-256 manifest

In `HANDOFF_TO_MASTER.md`, state clearly whether:

- T3 correctness was reproduced under the exact frozen contract;
- the dense preregistered storage crossover prediction was supported or falsified;
- sparse/orientation-adaptive layouts changed the practical picture;
- favorable cases occur naturally in independent external designs;
- any advantage survives full lifecycle accounting;
- any advantage survives credible optimized comparators.

A timing loss does not falsify T3 if its correctness and resource formulas survive. Conversely, a storage or timing win must not be promoted into a novelty claim or manuscript rewrite. Return the complete evidence to Master for the next convergence gate.
